votal site for arms manufacturing, particularly during the 19th century. The city's establishment was closely associated with the burgeoning Russian industrial revolution and was influenced by notable figures such as the Russian Emperor Peter the Great, who sought to modernize the Russian economy through industrialization. Zlatoust's development reflects the broader historical narrative of Russia's transition from a predominantly agrarian society to an industrial powerhouse.

